## Research
Research doc: docs/research/budget-exceeded-outcome-emission.md

Key findings:
- Approach validated with .90 confidence (up from .85 in parent research)
- Consumer compatibility audit: all 6 TASK_COMPLETE consumers verified SAFE
- AuditMapHook, RetrospectiveHook use outcome != success pattern (budget_exceeded correctly skipped)
- HookReactionRouter match predicates on outcome: failure naturally exclude budget_exceeded
- All existing test files use non-budget exceptions (RuntimeError, ValueError, LintGateError); none break
- Prior art: Celery dont_autoretry_for, Temporal non_retryable confirm the pattern
- depends_on 985 is a dangling reference (archived via SPLIT); real dependency is #984 (done)
- Task is independent of #991 and #992 per architecture review
- Implementation is ~5 LOC in reconcile_tasks plus TypedDict docstring update
- AC is complete and ready for TDD decomposition by architect

Sources: Celery task retry docs, Temporal failure detection docs
